            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 94,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "If it doesn't have units, it isn't a sensor.  You probably want to look at Metrics."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 94,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P. K. Lee",
                        "email": "p.k.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "PKLee-Quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "However, when retrieving sensor data via Modbus, we also need to obtain other non-sensor data, such as the device's serial number, firmware version, and service information. In this case, we can only use unclassified units. Do you have any suggestions?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 94,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Modbus might call them \"sensors\", IPMI might call them \"sensors\" but they are not a Sensor.Value.  They're other dbus objects.\n\nRedfish also doesn't allow unit-less sensors."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 94,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P. K. Lee",
                        "email": "p.k.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "PKLee-Quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, based on the logic of interface classification, you are correct. I need to come up with another solution. Thank you."
                }
            ],
